        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Giant stone monsters that serve Odium in the Desolations.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prelude" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "115" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Thunderclasts are about thirty feet tall, skeletal and humanoid, with long limbs ending in spiky claws, rib-like ridges on their chests and backs, and narrow, arrow-like heads with glowing red eyes.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "60" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "84" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite their size they stay upright easily and swing with enough force to topple fortifications, yet can throw boulders accurately or carry Fused in their hands.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "116" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "They do not crack and seem impossible to destroy by ordinary means, though hammers help, and Shardbearers can cut them apart until they can no longer move.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "prologue" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "120" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Though twisted, they keep enough personality to answer to names and have a sense of gender. They obey commands and roar and trumpet, but don't seem able to speak.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "120" }]
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
