              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Odium created the thunderclasts thousands of years before the True Desolation; they date back at least to Nohadon's time. People sent hunting parties after them, though only Radiants could fight them, and they threatened even the Heralds.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "60" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "51" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "After Aharietiam they passed into myth, likely surviving as stories of Voidbringers with bodies of stone.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "3" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "51" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In his visions Dalinar saw thunderclast corpses littering Nohadon's battlefield, and watched one rip itself out of the ground.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "60" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "epilogue" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The True Desolation",
          "revealedIn": [
